"PROGRAM: sargent\n"
"\n"
"USAGE: sargent [OPTIONS] <phenotypes> <input.trees> [<geno_prefix>]\n"
"\n"
"DESCRIPTION: Fit a Bayesian sparse linear mixed model incorporating ancestral\n"
"recombination graphs (ARGs).  Phenotypes are modelled as y = X*beta + u + eps\n"
"where X*beta is a BayesR fixed-effect component and u is a random effect whose\n"
"covariance is a weighted sum of local-tree kinship matrices from the ARG.\n"
"Inference is performed in two stages: (1) variational coordinate descent for\n"
"fixed effects; (2) REML-style updates for segment weights and residual variance.\n"
"\n"
"ARGUMENTS:\n"
"    <phenotypes>\n"
"        Phenotype file.  Each non-comment line should contain one phenotype\n"
"        value (the last whitespace-separated field on the line is used).\n"
"\n"
"    <input.trees>\n"
"        Tree sequence file (.trees).  Used for local-tree covariance matrices\n"
"        and, when --ts-geno is given, as the source of genotypes.\n"
"\n"
"    <geno_prefix>\n"
"        Prefix for PLINK BED files (<prefix>.bed, <prefix>.bim, <prefix>.fam).\n"
"        Required unless --ts-geno is specified.\n"
"\n"
"MAIN OPTIONS:\n"
"    --help, -h\n"
"        Display this help message and exit.\n"
"\n"
"    --version, -v\n"
"        Display the current version number and exit.\n"
"\n"
"    --silent, -z\n"
"        Omit all progress updates and per-iteration output to stderr.\n"
"\n"
"    --ts-geno, -G\n"
"        Obtain genotypes from the tree sequence file rather than a BED\n"
"        file.  When this option is given, <geno_prefix> must be omitted.\n"
"\n"
"    --fixed-only, -F\n"
"        Run Stage 1 (fixed-effects inference) only.  Produces\n"
"        <outroot>.beta.tsv but not <outroot>.w2.tsv.\n"
"\n"
"    --random-only, -R\n"
"        Run Stage 2 (random-effects inference) only, skipping Stage 1.\n"
"        Fixed effects are set to zero.  Produces <outroot>.w2.tsv but\n"
"        not <outroot>.beta.tsv.\n"
"\n"
"    --pi0 <val>, -P <val>\n"
"        Prior expected fraction of null segments (0 < val < 1).  Sets a\n"
"        Beta(1, pi0/(1-pi0)) hyperprior on the activation probability phi,\n"
"        giving prior mean phi=1-pi0 (e.g. --pi0 0.9 gives prior mean\n"
"        phi=0.1, favouring 90% null segments).  Default: Beta(1,1).\n"
"\n"
"    --outroot <prefix>, -o <prefix>\n"
"        Set the output file prefix (default: \"sargent\").  Output files\n"
"        are named <prefix>.beta.tsv and <prefix>.w2.tsv.\n"
"\n"
"ALGORITHMIC VARIANTS (for systematic comparison):\n"
"    --uniform-random, -U\n"
"        Replace Stage 2's per-tree REML with a single shared variance\n"
"        component on the uniformly-weighted kinship K = (1/S) sum_s G_s.\n"
"        Equivalent to fitting ARG-BLUP with a single tau^2.  Useful when\n"
"        per-tree weights are unidentifiable.\n"
"\n"
"    --em <N>, -E <N>\n"
"        Run joint variational coordinate descent for <N> outer iterations.\n"
"        Each outer iteration does ONE V-solve, ONE sweep of BayesR beta\n"
"        updates using V-aware precision (instead of sigma^2 I), and ONE\n"
"        REML EM step on ws^2 and sigma^2.  All updates share a common\n"
"        residual snapshot per iteration; refreshed at the start of the\n"
"        next iteration (manuscript-style mean-field VB).\n"
"        Initialised with beta=0 and warm uniform ws^2 so the first beta\n"
"        sweep sees a non-trivial random offset and cannot cannibalise.\n"
"        Polyak-Ruppert averaging on ws^2 and sigma^2 over the second half.\n"
"        Cannot be combined with --fixed-only or --random-only.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"OUTPUT FILES:\n"
"    <outroot>.beta.tsv\n"
"        Fixed-effect estimates.  Written after Stage 1 (or when both\n"
"        stages are run).  Columns: gamma_1 ... gamma_K  E_beta, where\n"
"        gamma_k is the posterior probability that SNP j belongs to\n"
"        mixture component k, and E_beta is the posterior expected value\n"
"        of beta_j.  One row per polymorphic SNP.\n"
"\n"
"    <outroot>.w2.tsv\n"
"        Segment-weight estimates.  Written after Stage 2 (or when both\n"
"        stages are run).  Columns: rho_1 ... rho_M  E_ws2, where rho_m\n"
"        is the posterior responsibility of component m for segment s, and\n"
"        E_ws2 is the posterior expected value of w_s^2.  One row per\n"
"        local tree (segment).\n"
"";
